course: dictionary
lesson: 15365
title: Job words: soundman
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A soundman is a person whose job is to record or control sound. Sound is what we hear: voices, music, footsteps and bangs. The word is made of two smaller words, sound and man, so you can often guess its meaning from its parts.
explain: «The soundman held the long microphone above the actors' heads.» The clue is microphone. A microphone records sound, so the soundman is the person who looks after the recording. Ask yourself: what job would need a microphone?
explain: Soundmen work on films, television, radio, concerts and plays. «The soundman turned the dial on the sound desk to make the music louder.» The sound desk is the panel where sound is controlled. Today people often say «sound engineer» or «sound technician», so the job fits women as well as men.
fact: A soundman is a person who records or controls sound.
fact: Soundmen work on films, television, radio, concerts and plays.
fact: «Soundman» is made of two words: sound and man.
fact: Today people often say «sound engineer», «sound technician» or «sound person».
fact: A sound desk is the panel where a sound person controls the sound.
exercise: Who is a soundman? | A person who sells tickets at a cinema | *A person who records or controls the sound for films, TV or plays | A person who drives the cameras | A person who paints the scenery for a play
exercise: «The soundman checked the microphone before the concert began.» Which modern word means the same as soundman? | *sound technician | lighting designer | bus driver | cake maker
exercise: «The soundman listened carefully through his headphones.» Which word in this sentence tells you the job is about hearing? | *listened | soundman | headphones | through
test: What might a soundman use to control the volume of a concert? | *A sound desk | A stage curtain | A paintbrush | A pair of scissors
test: Which job is a soundman most like? | A person who makes costumes for actors | *A person who records sound for a television programme | A person who fixes cars | A person who cuts hair in a salon
exam: Why does the word soundman fit a job about sound? | *Because it is made of sound and man, and the job is about sound | Because a soundman must be very tall | Because it means a person who paints scenery | Because it is an old word for a singer
